- id: "R2-N1"
  summary: "Title/framing promises general answer but experiments only cover SFT ≤3B"
  category: framing
  severity: critical
  status: resolved
  first_raised_round: 2
  last_seen_round: 6
  mentions:
    - {round: 2, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Table 2: vanilla 2PL MAE ≤ ContamCal on all benchmarks."}
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title still 'ContamCal'."}
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title promises decomposition but core result is nothing to decompose."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title changed to question form but framing still inconsistent."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Title question form improved but still over-scopes."}
    - {round: 8, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及。Title now 'Not All Models Are Inflated'."}
    - {round: 9, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。"}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。"}
    - {round: 11, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未直接提及。新 overclaiming concerns under R8-N3 and R11-N1."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未直接提及（fresh review）。Title framing itself resolved; overclaiming tracked under R11-N1."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 2, action: "Reframe paper", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 3, action: "Change title, rewrite Abstract/Contributions", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 4, action: "Reframe as empirical investigation", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 5, action: "Rewrite Introduction as question-driven", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 6, action: "Modify title to scope claim", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
  resolution: "Title changed to 'Not All Models Are Inflated'. Paper repositioned as empirical investigation."
  resolution_round: 7

- id: "R2-W6"
  summary: "SFT injection ecological validity insufficient — null finding may be SFT artifact"
  category: experiment
  severity: critical
  status: resolved
  first_raised_round: 2
  last_seen_round: 12
  mentions:
    - {round: 2, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Intro motivates with pretraining but experiments only SFT."}
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Limitations one sentence only."}
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Elevated to critical."}
    - {round: 9, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Limitations discussion still too brief."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "", note: "Section 6 includes Schaeffer et al. comparison."}
    - {round: 11, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Re-raised as part of R11-N1."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Re-raised as Should-Fix. Both reviewers note AUGMENT mode +33% data volume confound. Volume control only on Falcon3. Schaeffer et al. comparison in Section 6 exists but SFT vs pretraining mechanism discussion still insufficient."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 9, action: "Expand SFT discussion in Section 6", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
  resolution: "Section 6 rewritten with Schaeffer et al. comparison. Limitations includes SFT caveat."
  resolution_round: 9

- id: "R3-W10"
  summary: "Additive linear γ assumption untested"
  category: method
  severity: critical
  status: resolved
  first_raised_round: 3
  last_seen_round: 6
  mentions:
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1", note: "Linear γ may average down to non-significant."}
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Elevated to critical."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "R2 proposes threshold DGP simulation."}
    - {round: 8, reviewers: "", note: "DGP robustness appendix addresses this."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未直接提及（fresh review）。DGP simulation in Appendix addressed."}
  resolution: "400-run threshold DGP simulation completed. Appendix P written."
  resolution_round: 7

- id: "R4-N1"
  summary: "Domain-level γ significance — P(γ<0) inconsistency and Bonferroni claim unstable"
  category: method
  severity: critical
  status: open
  first_raised_round: 4
  last_seen_round: 12
  mentions:
    - {round: 4, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Bonferroni α=0.00625; CI upper bound likely includes zero."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Social Sciences at 99.1% does not pass Bonferroni."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "J=16 data available but main text still presents J=13."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "CONSENSUS Must-Fix. P(γ<0) inconsistency between §5.7 and Appendix K."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "R1", note: "R1-Minor-5 re-raises: Abstract cites 99.7% (default prior) without mentioning tight prior failure (99.35% < Bonferroni 99.375%). Selective reporting of most favorable number."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 4, action: "Report Bonferroni corrected results", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 6, action: "Switch main text to J=16 results", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 10, action: "Resolve P(γ<0) numerical inconsistency; mark γ conclusions exploratory", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "open"}

- id: "R3-N3"
  summary: "ARC PPP < 0.05 across all J — IRT results unreliable"
  category: method
  severity: warning
  status: in_progress
  first_raised_round: 3
  last_seen_round: 12
  mentions:
    - {round: 3, reviewers: "R1", note: "Within-family J=13 ARC PPP=0.003 not reported."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Table 3 now has PPP=0.003. Move ARC IRT to Appendix."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "MMLU PPP=0.16-0.25 only in Appendix, not main text."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "R1-N4 re-raises as critical: ARC PPP=0.003 but cross-benchmark conclusions still drawn. R2 agrees with nuance: §5.2 cross-benchmark direction is based on raw accuracy not IRT, so IRT failure doesn't invalidate direction findings. Both agree paper should explicitly separate raw-accuracy and IRT-based conclusions."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 9, action: "Add ARC PPP=0.003 discussion in main text", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 10, action: "Report MMLU PPP in main text", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "open"}
    - {round: 12, action: "Add explicit statement in §5.2 that cross-benchmark direction conclusions are based on raw accuracy, not IRT estimates", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "open"}

- id: "R2-W1"
  summary: "RRF multi-signal fusion — S2/S4 near-random signals retained despite evidence of harm"
  category: method
  severity: critical
  status: in_progress
  first_raised_round: 2
  last_seen_round: 12
  mentions:
    - {round: 2, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "RRF = S1 only."}
    - {round: 5, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "RRF ablation complete. Downgraded to warning."}
    - {round: 11, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "S2/S4 AUC≈0.48-0.51 (near random) retained without rationale. Minor."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "CONSENSUS Critical. Elevated from warning. R1-N1: S2 AUC≈0.48-0.50, S4≈0.47-0.51. Appendix E: removing S2 raises ρ_dose from 0.049→0.471 (S2 actively harmful at model level). 'item ρ=0.773' defense is circular (correlation with full RRF, not ground truth). R2 adds: Appendix AA shows S1-only AUC 0.93-0.99 while RRF drops to 0.73-0.93. However R2 notes S4 contributes 4.9× more to γ estimation than S2 (Appendix E γ ablation). Both agree: report S1-only pipeline as reference baseline."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 9, action: "Report s_ij classification performance", assigned_to: "main_agent", status: "done"}
    - {round: 12, action: "Report S1-only pipeline γ estimates and calibration MAE as oracle baseline; justify S2/S4 retention with ground-truth item-level AUC rather than self-referential rank correlation", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "open"}

- id: "R2-N2"
  summary: "CI coverage systematically abnormal"
  category: method
  severity: warning
  status: resolved
  first_raised_round: 2
  last_seen_round: 6
  mentions:
    - {round: 2, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Need coverage + root cause."}
    - {round: 6, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "Root cause diagnosis insufficient."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "", note: "本轮未提及（fresh review）。"}
