- id: "R8-N1"
  summary: "Cross-seed stability claims overstated — n=3 seeds insufficient for taxonomy validation"
  category: experiment
  severity: critical
  status: in_progress
  first_raised_round: 8
  last_seen_round: 12
  mentions:
    - {round: 8, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "n=3 seeds yields wide CIs; strict sign consistency only 2/5."}
    - {round: 10, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "n=3 acceptable given compute. Downgraded to Minor."}
    - {round: 11, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "CONSENSUS Major. Re-raised. n=3 has 12.5% spurious consistency risk."}
    - {round: 12, reviewers: "R1,R2", note: "CONSENSUS Critical. R1-N3: strict sign consistency 3/6; OLMo-2 CI [-0.55,+2.60] and Phi-4 CI [-0.17,+1.39] both cross zero. τ=2pp based on n=3 SD is circular (n=3 SD unstable, χ² df=2). Appendix Z parametric comparison: Gemma-2 and OLMo-2 Benefit indistinguishable from Constant (AICc). R2 strongly agrees: 'Benefit' for these families statistically = null effect. Both: downgrade taxonomy to 'exploratory typology' or increase to n≥5."}
  action_items:
    - {round: 8, action: "Increase seeds to n≥5 or weaken claims", assigned_to: "main_agent", status: "open"}
    - {round: 11, action: "Report p-value for directional test under H0", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "in_progress"}
    - {round: 12, action: "Acknowledge in main text that Gemma-2 and OLMo-2 Benefit are AICc-indistinguishable from null effect; either increase to n≥5 or relabel taxonomy as exploratory typology", assigned_to: "paper_agent", status: "open"}

